From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: ASoC: sunxi: h713-msp: a standby aborted before the island lost its power is rebuilt, not called a loss

msp_resume set the state to "error" after every standby that had run
msp_suspend, whether or not pd_tvfe was ever cut - and nothing rebuilt
the DSP then: h713-mips-restart runs only when the display MIPS was
parked, and the park comes in suspend_late, after msp_suspend. A standby
aborted between the two (a wake-up event while the devices went down -
the second press of the power key that h713-power keeps the projector on
for since TODO 5.14 U2) left a live island reported dead: the picture
on, no sound until the next successful standby or a reboot. Read in the
review of 09.10.2026 (TODO 5.16), confirmed in the code on 12.10.2026.

The resume now reads whether the power was lost - the TVFE router word
and the audio top's clock bits, which the bring-up sets and checks; both
read 0 after a real sleep (HY310, 09.10.2026) and neither read hangs -
and rebuilds a live island itself, through the same bring-up "echo 1 >
reset" runs (65 of 65 in the self-healing). A real loss stays "error",
with the message naming what rebuilds it.

To measure: pm_test=devices aborts after the devices' suspend phase,
before the park: state "running" afterwards, "standby aborted before the
island lost its power" in the log, then a real standby as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun50i-h713-msp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun50i-h713-msp.c
@@ -2524,6 +2524,25 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Did the island really lose its power? A standby that was aborted after
+ * msp_suspend but before the noirq phase (a wake-up event while the
+ * devices went down, review 09.10. and TODO 5.14 U2) never cut pd_tvfe:
+ * the DSP runs on with its patch and its graph, and only the bridge PCM
+ * was stopped. Read, not assumed: the TVFE router word and the audio top's
+ * clock bits, which the bring-up sets and checks (msp_island_up). Both
+ * survive only with the power; after a real sleep the top word reads 0
+ * (HY310, 09.10.2026). Neither read hangs - a dead demod bus reads 0.
+ */
+static bool msp_island_powered(struct h713_msp *msp)
+{
+	unsigned int router = 0;
+
+	if (regmap_read(msp->router, 0, &router) || !router)
+		return false;
+	return (readl(msp->top + MSP_TOP_CTL) & MSP_TOP_CTL_CLK) == MSP_TOP_CTL_CLK;
+}
+
 static int msp_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct h713_msp *msp = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
@@ -2536,9 +2555,22 @@
 		msp->heal_after_sleep = true;
 		schedule_work(&msp->heal);
 		dev_info(dev, "standby: the DSP is rebuilt after the wake\n");
+	} else if (msp->lost_in_sleep && msp_island_powered(msp)) {
+		/*
+		 * The sleep never reached the island: rebuild what suspend
+		 * took down - the same bring-up "echo 1 > reset" runs, on a
+		 * live island, as the self-healing has run it (65 of 65) -
+		 * rather than report a loss that did not happen and leave
+		 * the picture without sound until somebody resets by hand.
+		 */
+		msp->state = MSP_STATE_ERROR;
+		msp->heal_count = 0;
+		msp->heal_after_sleep = true;
+		schedule_work(&msp->heal);
+		dev_info(dev, "standby aborted before the island lost its power: the DSP is rebuilt\n");
 	} else if (msp->lost_in_sleep) {
 		msp->state = MSP_STATE_ERROR;
-		dev_info(dev, "standby: the DSP lost its power in the sleep and is not rebuilt (rebuild_after_sleep=0): state error, no HDMI audio until a reboot\n");
+		dev_info(dev, "standby: the DSP lost its power in the sleep and is not rebuilt by the driver (rebuild_after_sleep=0): state error until h713-mips-restart or \"echo 1 > reset\" rebuilds it\n");
 	}
 	msp->lost_in_sleep = false;
 	mutex_unlock(&msp->lock);
